ls, shared platform capabilities, or core product experiences - but you do not build tech/platform for its own sake. You see strong platform design as a way to help users move faster, create better products, and unlock new business models. You are opinionated, thoughtful, and execution-oriented. You can focus a team on the few decisions that matter most, create momentum in ambiguous situations, and ship products that raise the bar for both quality and impact. Minimum requirements 7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time owning platform, API, or developer-facing products end to end Demonstrated ability to own a product area end to end: setting strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes Strong analytical instincts and comfort defining the measurement framework before you ship Clear written communication and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels Preferred qualifications Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available platform capabilities A track record of making well-judged foundational investments ahead of user demand	{}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8065034	2026-09-06 11:03:38.769	2026-10-31 17:30:13.173	t	2026-10-31 17:30:13.169
