gislative environments Deep expertise in financial services regulation and payments policy, with a strong understanding of the legislative and regulatory landscape across banking, money transmission, and digital assets Familiarity with, and ideally direct experience on, emerging technology policy — including artificial intelligence, agentic commerce, and the regulatory questions that arise at the intersection of AI and financial services Strong relationships with policymakers and staff on both sides of the aisle and a reputation for credibility, reliability, and good judgment A proven track record of managing complex, technical policy issues — capable of managing major initiatives independently, driving coalitions, or project managing a cross-functional team Excellent judgment — capable of making smart decisions in the face of ambiguity and imperfect information and learning from them A terrific communicator and writer, adept at working with lawyers, regulators, engineers, business teams, and colleagues to make complex concepts clear and understandable Passion for Stripe&#39;s mission of helping businesses grow and thrive A collaborative, curious team-first mindset with experience thriving in ambiguous, high-growth or startup environments across global offices. Empathy, humility, and a respect for those who have views that are different from yours A willingness to work with a diverse group of policy, regulatory, and product professionals who care deeply about Stripe&#39;s policy issues, our users, and each other Willingness to travel 25% for meetings and events.	{git}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8070044	2026-09-06 11:03:39.172	2026-10-31 17:30:13.591	f	2026-09-06 11:03:39.171
