 evaluation through technical validation, implementation, activation, and post-launch expansion. Monitor adoption and payment volume after launch, identify barriers and whitespace, and coordinate with account teams on growth plans. Serve as an internal and customer-facing LPM expert, creating field enablement, account-planning guidance, and repeatable regional sales plays. Synthesize market intelligence and user feedback for Product, Engineering, Partnerships, and Marketing to help inform product and go-to-market priorities. Who you are We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. Minimum requirements 5+ years of experience in sales, business development, partnerships, or a closely related commercial role at a technology company, with a track record of strong performance against goals. Experience leading complex B2B sales cycles involving multiple business, commercial, and technical stakeholders. Ability to understand technical product requirements and translate them into clear customer outcomes and commercially viable solutions. Strong executive presence and the ability to communicate effectively with product and engineering teams, operational leaders, and C-level executives. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships and influence cross-functional teams without direct authority. Experience developing business cases and leading complex commercial negotiations. A self-starting, highly organized approach and the ability to deliver results in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment. Excellent written, verbal, presentation, and analytical skills. Willingness to travel approximately 10% of the time for user meetings, team events, sales kickoffs, and occasional international business needs. Preferred qualifications Experience in payments, alternative payment methods, ecommerce, or financial technology. Knowledge of payment preferences and commerce trends across North America or Latin America. Experience working in a product-sales overlay model alongside account executives, customer success teams, or technical sellers. Familiarity with product-led integrations and complex customer organizational or account structures. Experience helping businesses enter new markets, localize payment experiences, or improve checkout conversion.	{go}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8190036	2026-10-31 17:29:20.544	2026-10-31 17:30:10.454	t	2026-10-31 17:30:10.451
