m owns, including diagnosing production issues and improving them based on what we learn. Who you are We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. Minimum requirements 3+ years of professional software-development experience, including meaningful experience building and shipping mobile applications or SDKs. Experience developing for at least one major mobile platform using technologies such as Kotlin or Java for Android. Strong software-design fundamentals and experience creating maintainable APIs, components, or frameworks. Experience delivering mobile functionality beyond an isolated UI layer for example, integrating with APIs and services, handling local state, or working with device capabilities. Experience testing, debugging, monitoring, and improving mobile software in production. Ability to collaborate effectively with engineering, product, design, and other technical and non-technical partners. A demonstrated commitment to building high-quality user and developer experiences. Preferred qualifications Experience building mobile SDKs, shared libraries, or developer-facing APIs used outside your immediate team. Experience with both iOS and Android, or with cross-platform technologies such as React Native or Kotlin Multiplatform. Experience with camera, image-processing, document-capture, biometrics, or other device-integrated mobile experiences. Experience designing mobile software that handles sensitive data and applies security and privacy principles by default. Familiarity with accessibility, internationalization, mobile performance, and unreliable network conditions. Experience with mobile CI, automated testing, release automation, observability, or developer-productivity tooling. Experience contributing to backend APIs or services that support mobile products. Ability to simplify complex re