oss-functional partners to determine the safest path forward. Responsibilities Manage community interactions across supported platforms while consistently meeting quality, productivity, and responsiveness expectations. Act as an escalation point for complex, sensitive, ambiguous, or high-visibility community cases, including influential users, executive tags, media-adjacent attention, rapid amplification, cross-platform misinformation, and privacy or brand concerns. Support teammates as they navigate complex cases by providing actionable feedback and explaining the reasoning behind recommended responses and escalation decisions. Recognize potential social-media incidents or high-risk situations and engage a senior Specialist or incident lead before making a novel or material-risk public commitment. Participate in incident response under senior Specialist guidance, maintaining clear ownership and communication. Gather relevant facts, identify stakeholders and risks, consider response options, and recommend a safe path forward for escalated cases. Use dashboards, queue reviews, social-listening reports, and basic operational data to identify patterns and support decisions; develop familiarity with basic queries where helpful. Communicate clear product, user, and risk signals to cross-functional partners such as Product, Risk, Comms, and Docs. Contribute to trend summaries, incident retrospectives, product-signal reports, playbooks, and internal knowledge resources. Own defined components of pre-scoped improvement projects, maintaining a plan and communicating progress, dependencies, blockers, and risks. Capture reusable lessons from escalations and share them through team documentation and knowledge-sharing forums. Who you are We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. Preferred qualifications are helpful but not required. Minimum requirements Experience in public-facing support, community operations, technical support,