, playbooks, reference architectures, and execution standards across the monetization-to-revenue-reporting lifecycle, including subscription management, usage-based and hybrid billing, invoicing, tax, revenue recognition, and analytics Advise executives, developers, architects, finance leaders, and other decision-makers on modernizing their monetization and revenue-management architectures Guide strategic customers from business and technical discovery through solution design, validation, adoption, value realization, and expansion Translate recurring customer needs, market signals, and deal friction into actionable insights that influence Product and Engineering priorities Represent the Revenue SSA organization in global leadership forums, providing clear perspectives on performance, capacity, risks, customer needs, and growth opportunities Shape the Revenue Suite go-to-market approach across every region, accounting for regional regulatory requirements, business models, and market-specific billing practices Build strong collaboration and knowledge-sharing mechanisms across regional and global teams to improve consistency, reuse, and execution quality Advance Stripe&#39;s external thought leadership through executive briefings, industry events, white papers, and reference architectures focused on billing, monetization, tax automation, and revenue management Who you are We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. Minimum requirements 15+ years of experience in technical sales, solutions architecture, solution consulting, or another customer-facing technical role in enterprise technology 10+ years of experience building and scaling pre-sales or solutions architecture teams, including hiring, managing, coaching, and developing senior individual contributors Experience managing managers, with a trac