ation, adoption, and durable operational handoff. A player-coach mindset: high ownership, sound judgment, adaptability under pressure, and a collaborative, hands-on approach that sets a high bar for quality. Experience establishing goals, work plans, operating cadences, decision forums, and success measures for initiatives spanning regions, segments, product lines, and multiple stakeholders. Strong judgment in prioritizing competing demands and allocating limited team capacity to the highest-value work. Ability to navigate senior stakeholders with differing incentives and decision rights; drive alignment while making trade-offs and escalation paths explicit. Proven ability to structure qualitative and quantitative inputs into clear recommendations, assess program health and risk, and guide prioritization with data. Strong executive communication skills, including facilitation of senior working sessions and decision-oriented reporting. Preferred qualifications Experience managing competitive programs, strategic-account programs, product-launch programs, commercial transformation, or other high-stakes GTM initiatives. Experience building a new operating model, program-management team, or repeatable playbook from the ground up. Experience partnering closely with Product, Product Operations, PMM, Sales, Pricing, Finance &amp; Strategy, Market Intelligence, and GTM Systems. Familiarity with competitive intelligence, win/loss analysis, sales enablement, pricing, commercial strategy, product-feedback mechanisms, or executive account programs. Experience at a B2B technology, enterprise software, fintech, payments, or platform company; comfort using SQL, BI tools, or similar methods to analyze pipeline, adoption, revenue, and operational data.	{go,sql}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8175671	2026-09-06 11:03:37.202	2026-10-31 17:30:11.788	t	2026-10-31 17:30:11.785
