w we win self-serve users in international markets and then make it real—turning funnel data and customer insight into a sequenced roadmap, and shipping the experiments and features that move the metrics. The right person for this role thinks like a growth PM and a founder: you&#39;re fluent in funnels and experimentation, you have genuine taste for 0-to-1 product, and you move fast under ambiguity. You bring deep user empathy to localizing Stripe with contextual relevance, and you think in systems and platforms—turning experimental features into scaled growth levers What you&#39;ll do Own the self-serve growth roadmap: identify the highest-leverage opportunities to grow activation across our ex-US markets, and build the case for investment Build a deep understanding of our customers—from bootstrapped solopreneurs to well-funded founders—synthesizing funnel metrics, experiment results, and time in the product into sharp hypotheses about what will drive growth Partner with engineering to ship—you&#39;ll drive specs, prioritization, and execution with a high degree of hands-on involvement, and run experiments to build conviction in your roadmap Scale what works: take wins proven in small samples and roll them out through our localization and recommendation platforms, so the right experience reaches each market and use case Collaborate with Stripe&#39;s global product teams to ensure regional needs are reflected in platform decisions, and advocate for regional investment at the right moments Who you are You have 7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time spent shipping 0-to-1 products You reason from first principles—breaking ambiguous growth problems down to fundamentals, forming a sharp point of view, and moving fast under uncertainty with the ownership of a founder You&#39;re data-savvy: fluent in funnels, metrics, and experimentation, you let the numbers sharpen your instincts, and you know when a test earns conviction and when it only adds noise You have strong product taste and are technically comfortable—you sweat the details of a localized experience (message clarity, contextual guidance) and can engage credibly with engineers on API design and system tradeoffs You&#39;re an exceptional communicator—verbal and written—who can influence without authority across a matrixed organization You&#39;re based in Singapore or have a strong reason to be Why Stripe Stripe is still early in its presence outside the US, which means the person in this role will have genuine influence over how we show up in some of the world&#39;s most important emerging markets. You&#39;ll have the scope of a startup with the resources of a company that processes hundreds of billions of dollars a year.	{}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8267105	2026-10-31 17:29:22.435	2026-10-31 17:30:12.27	t	2026-10-31 17:30:12.266
a02db7ab-b713-4ab7-b4ee-1f0e5c1c4ef0	8165137	GREENHOUSE	Product Manager, Identity & Access Management	stripe	US-Remote, US-Chicago	Who we are About Stripe Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career. About the team IAM is the nerve center of Stripe. We control how millions of businesses grant access to their account, including employees, AI agents, apps, and API integrations, across the Dashboard, API, CLI, and MCP. We&#39;re also a platform team, building the unified, fine-grained permissions model that every product at Stripe builds on. AI agents are changing how businesses operate, and how they get authorized, governed, and secured is being defined right now—largely by us. We’re tackling challenging and unsolved problems for real businesses, like how to model agents when they blur the line between acting on behalf of a human vs. standalone principals, or how to authorize entire agent workflows rather than step-by-step actions. We’re collaborating directly with the frontier AI labs on the evolution of MCP, new identity protocols, and agent integrations. We build for solo founders and Fortune 500s alike, and the tension between those two is where the real product work lives. What you’ll do You&#39;ll set the vision and drive the roadmap for how every principal, human, agent, or app, gets access to a Stripe account. You&#39;ll do it by talking directly to the founders, admins, and developers who use it. Design the experience of granting access, everywhere. Signing up, inviting a teammate, creating an API key, authorizing an agent or a third-party app. Design for agents specifically. Design for agents as a new principal within Stripe, including how they authenticate, what they&#39;re allowed to do, and how businesses stay in control, including approvals and human-in-the-loop checkpoints for actions involving real money. You&#39;re defining an experience that will set the industry standard. Drive least privilege, made easy. Take holistic ownership across Stripe to ensure that every user, app and agent has only the permissions it requires. Build custom roles, smart permission defaults, and permission recommendations based on real API usage to make least-privilege authorization easy rather than tedious. Push toward a world without secrets. Make secretless authentication (Workload Identity Federation) the default way developers integrate with Stripe to prevent emerging security threats from increasingly sophisticated and AI-powered attackers. Partner across all of Stripe. Pitch an ambitious vision, then get teams across Dashboard, API Platform, Security, Payments and Money Movement genuinely excited to build it with you. Who you are The hardest part of this job, and the most fun, is the constant trade-off: usability vs. security, flexibility vs. simplicity. It takes taste to find a shape that feels effortless for a solo founder and holds up at Fortune 500 scale. Minimum requirements 5+ years in PM, shipping platform or infrastructure products that other teams build on Background in security, identity, auth, or developer platforms, or serious curiosity about the space A habit of talking to users to find the real problem, not the reported one Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on authorization and authentication design A bias toward experimentation over big-bang launches Comfort setting direction in a space that&#39;s still being invented, across teams you don&#39;t manage	{go}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8165137	2026-09-06 11:03:37.665	2026-10-31 17:30:12.273	t	2026-10