duct, and Stripe’s security org to move fast without compromising safety. Minimum Requirements Have 8+ years of experience in Security GRC, ideally with time spent in fast-paced startup environments where you’ve built security practices from the ground up. Have a startup mindset: you’re scrappy, pragmatic, and move quickly to solve the most critical problems. You’re proficient with NIST CSF, OCC’s Cybersecurity Supervision Work Program and/or FFIEC IT Examination Handbook or other similar global frameworks. Proven prior experience with regulatory audits from Global auditors across Security domains. Thrive in ambiguity and know how to ruthlessly prioritize. Can balance security rigor with speed, especially in fast-moving environments. Demonstrated history converting complex policy, audit, and regulatory mandates into actionable operational and engineering controls. Broad technical depth across cloud architecture, identity management, appsec, data protection, and incident response operations. A track record of evaluating control environments, uncovering underlying risks, and executing sensible, long-term solutions. Strong program execution skills: crafting strategic roadmaps, setting milestones, navigating cross-team blockers, and driving remediation projects to completion. A collaborative approach to partnering across engineering, product, compliance, legal, and audit teams. Preferred Qualifications Have experience building or scaling security programs through execution, either at a startup or in an embedded role. Are excited about the potential of crypto and stablecoins to power global financial infrastructure (you don’t need deep prior knowledge—just curiosity and openness to learn).	{}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8237244	2026-10-31 17:29:22.851	2026-10-31 17:30:12.738	t	2026-10-31 17:30:12.734
