ld strong working relationships across Risk and Product, and help align teams when trade-offs or ambiguity arise Develop expertise that can support adjacent product-risk areas over time, including fraud Who you are You are comfortable working in ambiguous spaces where products, risks, and processes are still being defined. You can reason through risk scenarios, bring structure to complex questions, and work with technical partners to turn recommendations into scalable solutions. You are also motivated by improving how work gets done. You do not only identify risks. You look for ways to make risk assessment, decision-making, and monitoring more automated, consistent, and useful for the teams building Stripe products. Minimum requirements 5+ years of experience in risk, financial services, fintech, product strategy, data, or a related field Experience partnering with cross-functional teams, especially Product, Engineering, Data Science, Operations, or Partnerships Strong analytical judgment and the ability to turn complex information into clear recommendations and next steps Familiarity with and a keen interest in building and applying automation, tools, or agent-based workflows to improve processes and outcomes Experience using data to investigate problems, assess performance, or inform decisions Ability to communicate clearly with a range of stakeholders and build alignment across teams with different priorities Preferred qualifications Experience assessing risk for new products, product launches, or material product changes Experience in payments, product risk, platform risk, fraud, or financial crimes Experience using and building agentic workflows and using AI tools to simplify processes Experience with SQL, data analysis, data science workflows, or building operational tools Experience working with technical teams to define requirements and improve internal systems or processes Familiarity with risk-control design, monitoring, or policy development	{sql}	\N	http