levant projects and ideas that could result in the optimal broad-spectrum preventative. Help update our RFP material and/or launch specialized calls based on the current state of the field/portfolio. Diligence pipeline opportunities. Support early and deep / technical diligence of our grant and equity pipeline: evaluating science quality, development plans, team, and fit against our TPP. Engage a network of experts and primary literature to keep our strategy current. Engage networks (researchers, investors, founders, funders, etc.) to track research priorities, forecast trends, and identify cutting edge areas of science that Intercept should pursue. Who you are We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement. Minimum requirements Must have a PhD and/or MD in immunology and/or infectious disease with 3+ years of post-grad work experience (post-doc, academia, biotech, pharma, VC, or consulting) Demonstrated capacity to explore and evaluate a broad range of scientific topics and experience with scientific curation (e.g., oversight of a research portfolio, grant making experience, investment experience, etc.) Experience with the grant process, either success with receiving grant funding or awarding grants Familiar with early-stage product development, ideally with some experience / contribution Experience with project management from launch to completion / project quarterback with a high openness to getting hands dirty Extremely self-directed, diligent, very fast learner, excellent communicator, very action oriented (vs talking about things) Compelled by our mission to greatly reduce the burden of and risks from respiratory viruses Preferred qualifications Experience with capital allocation, either with grants and/or investments Experience with portfolio management, including portfolio construction and post-award management Direct product development experience (optimally with candidate nomination, CMC, IND-enabling studies, and Ph I trial launch)	{}	\N	https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=8060152	2026-09-06 11:03:38.225	2026-10-31 17:30:13.591	f	2026-09-06 11:03:38.223
